Experimental Physics I and II — MIT Junior Lab (@em-juniorlab: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_55H9HGYP31B14NSEEAZY27PW5E
MIT 8.13/8.14 teaching and technical teams, Fall 2016 and Spring 2017. [Complete public experimental course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/8-13-14-experimental-physics-i-ii-junior-lab-fall-2016-spring-2017/).

Study the full applicable experiment guides, apparatus descriptions, notebooks, uncertainty treatment and reporting expectations. Johnson/shot noise and radio measurement are especially useful electromagnetic investigations. Optical pumping and magnetic resonance connect to additional quantum knowledge; distinguish that requirement explicitly.

The course and resource categories were checked on 29 October 2026. Apparatus access, instruction and supervision are not supplied by a PDF; a literature reconstruction is different evidence from a physical experiment. OCW uses CC BY-NC-SA with component exceptions. Whole unrelated experiments are not prerequisites to every electromagnetic question, but an advanced experimental study must engage complete methods, not only a demonstration video.

**Return:** [Electromagnetic sources — complete books, courses, methods and research](../Sources.lingua#r_6XW0N80NM6WSDWED10N8N7WX3P).
